WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.111 --> 00:00:01.007
(audience clapping)

00:00:01.007 --> 00:00:03.321
- All right, well do you wanna hear her?

00:00:03.321 --> 00:00:05.930
You gotta sit down at
some point, you gotta sit.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.310
That's amazing. Does that
happen like in Target?

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.930
Like--
- No, no.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.017
- You just walk in and you are like,

00:00:11.017 --> 00:00:11.953
"well thank you, I arrived, I did."

00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:14.770
- Half the time, they
are like, "is that her?"

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.012
- That's always, they never--

00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:17.660
- I've never, sweats and everything, yes.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.160
- But, we're both from Texas.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.100
You recently were in Texas again, right?

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:21.996
- [Selena] Yeah

00:00:21.996 --> 00:00:22.829
- Because you don't live
there anymore, right?

00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:25.130
- No, I have a house there for, you know,

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.700
if I wanna go see family and
stuff because I still do.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.860
But, I've slowly moved my
family out here so it's working.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:31.782
- Clever.

00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:32.615
(laughs)

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:34.690
- But yeah, I just for some
reason I wanted to back

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.400
to my middle school, I wanted to go back

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.760
to my childhood home,
which I do often, and--

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.468
Oh yeah, that was me bothering the class.

00:00:41.468 --> 00:00:43.020
(audience laughs)

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.865
And I got to just be there
and say, you know like,

00:00:45.865 --> 00:00:49.500
I was here and I never ever
thought that I could be

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.130
where I am now.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.790
It was just really neat to see.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.400
And my teachers remembered
me and one of them

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.280
just ripped me, she was like,
"I remember she was like,

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.760
I'm gonna go do this movie.
I was like yeah, right.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.950
She just wanted to lie
and get out of school."

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.197
- That was, I went back to my school.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:07.307
I remember my algebra
teacher, Miss Tover, was like,

00:01:07.307 --> 00:01:09.140
"who you gonna, how are
you gonna know what they're

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.740
doing with your money, if
you're gonna make all this money

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.578
when you're old."

00:01:11.578 --> 00:01:12.590
I was like, "I'll pay someone
to do it and hope they

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:13.428
don't screw me over."

00:01:13.428 --> 00:01:14.340
(laughing)

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.173
- [Selena] Exactly.

00:01:15.173 --> 00:01:16.267
- I was like, and then I
saw her and I was like,

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.385
"still hoping!"

00:01:17.385 --> 00:01:18.530
(laughing)

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.363
It was like, I don't know.

00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:21.580
But you went to your childhood
home, is that kind of

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.413
special for you?

00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:23.246
- [Selena] Yeah.

00:01:23.246 --> 00:01:24.079
- Like where you grew up.

00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:26.140
- It was so, well I try to go there often,

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.630
just because it's nostalgic for me.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.130
And I've gone every year or so.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.117
Well, there's me!

00:01:33.117 --> 00:01:33.950
(laughing)

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.010
But I grew up there and
everything started from there.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.840
So I actually got to knock
on the door and someone

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.530
was finally there, because
no one's ever there.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.877
It was just this chilled
dude and he's like,

00:01:44.877 --> 00:01:46.050
"yeah, come look around."

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.960
He was so unfazed that I was there,

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.680
He's like, "yeah apparently
you wrote on this wall."

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:54.669
He goes, "also there's a crib
in the garage if you want it."

00:01:54.669 --> 00:01:55.632
- [Kelly] What?
- I was like, "my crib?"

00:01:55.632 --> 00:01:57.410
He was like, "yeah."

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.580
I was like, "my crib is in your garage?"

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.550
He goes, "yeah."

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.880
I was like, "can I have it?"

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.713
He goes, "sure"

00:02:02.713 --> 00:02:05.107
I'm like, he has all this stuff.

00:02:05.107 --> 00:02:08.133
And I had written in the
closets that I was in love with

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.392
Cole Sprouse.

00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:10.225
(audience laughs)

00:02:10.225 --> 00:02:12.413
- [Kelly] I am older
than you, who is that?

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:16.950
- Cole Sprouse was on "Sweet
Life With Zack And Cody".

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:17.783
- Okay, I know that, yes.

00:02:17.783 --> 00:02:19.790
- And I was obsessed with that show.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.822
And I thought we were
gonna be together, one day.

00:02:22.822 --> 00:02:24.060
(laughs)

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.380
- Then I guest starred on the
show, but I kissed his brother

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.658
and I didn't get to kiss Cole.

00:02:28.658 --> 00:02:30.450
(audience sighs)

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.390
- I always feel bad for y'all.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.200
I hate acting so like, I
don't know how you do it.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.084
- He was my first kiss.

00:02:35.084 --> 00:02:36.010
- Like, you don't know where
their mouths have been.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:36.945
Oh my gosh!

00:02:36.945 --> 00:02:37.778
- Yeah!

00:02:37.778 --> 00:02:38.611
(audience laughs)

00:02:38.611 --> 00:02:40.902
- Your first kiss was
with a stranger and actor?

00:02:40.902 --> 00:02:42.749
That's fine!
- On camera!

00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:43.582
(laughing)

00:02:43.582 --> 00:02:44.504
- Oh my God!

00:02:44.504 --> 00:02:45.337
- It was one of the worst days of my life.

00:02:45.337 --> 00:02:47.900
- You know what, mine wasn't
acting and it wasn't camera.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.733
Mine was horrible.

00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:50.673
It was like he was searching
for something with his tongue.

00:02:50.673 --> 00:02:51.506
It was, yeah.

00:02:51.506 --> 00:02:52.339
- Oh gosh!

00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:53.172
(audience gasps)

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.005
- I was like, "there's nothing in there,

00:02:54.005 --> 00:02:55.040
it's just my mouth."

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.440
like, and I literally went
and spit in his bathroom,

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.273
it was horrible.

00:02:58.273 --> 00:03:01.660
You said that this album
is your most honest album.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.709
So why do you think so?

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:06.780
- Because I started so young,
there's a huge part of me

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.060
that didn't get a chance
to develop my identity in a

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.540
normal setting.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.190
So when I was working with
Disney, it was the best time

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:17.850
of my life and I had a great
time, I had nothing but

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:18.683
good things to say.

00:03:18.683 --> 00:03:21.670
But it was a bit more controlled.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:24.530
There were certain things
that I was, you know,

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:29.237
kind of had to do and not maybe, go into,

00:03:29.237 --> 00:03:32.010
like figuring out what my sound would be.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.870
So I've constantly been
trying to make my music

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.080
better and better because, you know,

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.000
I know that people may
not think that I'm the

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.870
greatest singer but I
just worked my ass off and

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:47.710
I love, I really love
writing and creating.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.610
And creating melodies and growing.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:53.700
And I felt like this was my
chance to say all the things

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.010
that I wanted to say in that way,

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.023
which was talking about
relationships, and talking about

00:03:59.023 --> 00:04:02.270
difficult times, or being vulnerable,

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:05.530
or being stuck in your head.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.920
Because, you know, I can do that a lot.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.520
But I wanted it to feel good.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.400
You know, I wanted it to
feel like every word mattered

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.500
and you could feel it physically.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.410
And I'm still in the studio actually now,

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.750
because I feel like it's
inspired me and I just

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:21.583
wanna keep going.

00:04:21.583 --> 00:04:22.416
- A creative time, yeah.

00:04:22.416 --> 00:04:23.249
- [Selena] Yeah.

00:04:23.249 --> 00:04:24.082
- Ain't that funny, you make an album,

00:04:24.082 --> 00:04:24.915
that always happens with me too.

00:04:24.915 --> 00:04:26.650
I make an album and then
after I'm releasing it,

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.160
like right while I'm doing
it, I'm doing another one.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:28.993
- [Selena] Yeah exactly.

00:04:28.993 --> 00:04:29.826
- It always happens like that.

00:04:29.826 --> 00:04:30.659
- I'm like, I don't just--

00:04:30.659 --> 00:04:33.095
- But I wanna point something out because,

00:04:33.095 --> 00:04:36.110
doing the voice especially,
has been really interesting

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.817
because a lot of people
always think, 'cause you said

00:04:37.817 --> 00:04:39.266
"I know people might not
say I'm the best singer"

00:04:39.266 --> 00:04:42.600
The best singer in the
world, talking to everyone

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.627
in the world right now, is not
the loudest, and is not the

00:04:45.627 --> 00:04:48.080
"oh my God you've just sang
Whitney Houston" every time

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:48.913
you get.

00:04:48.913 --> 00:04:51.340
The best singers in the world move you.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.520
And that comes from all
different sounds and styles.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.800
So like, from a singer to a singer,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.490
it's beautiful what you
do and I love your record

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.100
and I love big, huge songs.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.100
But I love singing your music,

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.680
it means something and it moves people.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.932
So don't ever negate your
gift, because it's powerful.

00:05:07.932 --> 00:05:08.765
- [Selena] Thank you.

00:05:08.765 --> 00:05:09.598
(audience claps)

00:05:09.598 --> 00:05:10.431
(audience cheers)

00:05:10.431 --> 00:05:11.264
- That's what I wanted to say to that.

00:05:11.264 --> 00:05:12.097
(audience clapping)

00:05:12.097 --> 00:05:15.500
but whenever I first heard
"Rare" I was in a car

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.080
and I was listening to
Spotify or something.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.490
And I was like, "what?"

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.354
And I knew it was you
'cause I got all your music"

00:05:20.354 --> 00:05:23.690
but I was like, "what is this whole idea."

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:27.650
like, as a writer myself,
what a concept that nobody's

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.483
ever done.

00:05:28.483 --> 00:05:29.316
- Thank you.

00:05:29.316 --> 00:05:30.940
Like, I mean, why did
that, did that word just

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:31.800
stick out for you?

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.170
- Yeah, I felt like, you
know, that song actually

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.640
came into fruition four years ago so.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:38.473
- Wow.

00:05:38.473 --> 00:05:40.910
- It stuck with me throughout
creating this album

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.217
because, I like the kinda song that says,

00:05:44.217 --> 00:05:45.471
"look, I'm not perfect."

00:05:45.471 --> 00:05:48.668
You know, but I do know
that I deserve the best.

00:05:48.668 --> 00:05:49.501
- I'm special though.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:52.670
- Yeah, and I think that is
so, it's such an important

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:53.503
thing to say.

00:05:53.503 --> 00:05:55.390
It's like, I need that.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.830
You know, I've compared
myself to people for years

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.370
and if feel like I'm, you
know, sometimes get insecure

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.710
and I get, you know, I
go through normal things.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.750
And it's just that word
means so much to me,

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.340
because that's exactly what it means.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.531
It means that every single
person wasn't meant to be

00:06:11.531 --> 00:06:13.684
like everybody else, kind of thing.

00:06:13.684 --> 00:06:14.517
- Yeah.

00:06:14.517 --> 00:06:16.110
- Like you were saying to
me, wow I guess I'm now

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.152
saying it back myself.

00:06:17.152 --> 00:06:17.985
(audience laughs)

00:06:17.985 --> 00:06:22.520
But it's true, you know,
you are each created to be

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.180
who you are meant to be,
and that's that, you know.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:27.590
- And I think until you
believe that you are rare,

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:28.520
no one else will.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.353
- [Selena] Yeah.

00:06:29.353 --> 00:06:30.260
- And that's what I love about it.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.800
It's an empowering anthem.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.283
Like I love, I love, like
I told you in the room.

00:06:34.283 --> 00:06:36.766
It takes a lot to get me on a treadmill.

00:06:36.766 --> 00:06:39.190
And I'm like, "I've
gotta have a good record"

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.830
And I've been jamming your
record literally, just non-stop.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.460
So it's a really great record.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:44.933
But you also have a new beauty line,

00:06:44.933 --> 00:06:46.560
and it's called "Rare Beauty"

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.393
- Yeah.

00:06:47.393 --> 00:06:48.226
- [Kelly] Rare Beauty.

00:06:48.226 --> 00:06:49.100
(audience cheers)

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.470
- I cannot wait to try
it, 'cause I'm actually

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.019
highly allergic to a lot of makeup.

00:06:53.019 --> 00:06:55.768
But what got you into the beauty world?

00:06:55.768 --> 00:06:59.630
- At first off I had such
a connection with my fans,

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:02.430
and most of the time it's
talking about real things

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.100
that they're experiencing.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:07.870
And when I wanted to do this
thing, I wanted to actually

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.010
create a lifestyle with it.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:13.070
I wanted a line that was simple,

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.863
and that was hyper-allergenic.

00:07:16.821 --> 00:07:17.654
- [Kelly] Thank you.

00:07:17.654 --> 00:07:18.882
- And not tested on animals, nothing.

00:07:18.882 --> 00:07:22.970
I wanted it to feel like
every girl can wear it,

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:24.230
whoever wants to wear it.

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.900
But you could also build coverage.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:28.290
So it's simple stuff to
just help you know how to do

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:29.510
the go-to thing.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.533
And it's beautiful and it's encouraging.

00:07:33.432 --> 00:07:35.320
You know, I have so many
ideas for it to come,

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.578
where it can just be something powerful,

00:07:37.578 --> 00:07:39.400
or people can feel good.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.470
- Yeah, it is nice 'cause
I didn't grow up knowing

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.303
how to do makeup.

00:07:42.303 --> 00:07:44.067
There's a lot of girls that
aren't, we're like tomboys

00:07:44.067 --> 00:07:45.310
and like, didn't do that.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.307
So, it's really cool.
- Yeah this is super easy,

00:07:47.307 --> 00:07:50.110
- And you have such a huge
fan base of women too,

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.340
and I love that you're not
just about the aesthetics,

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.347
you're also about what's
inside that counts.

00:07:54.347 --> 00:07:55.180
- [Selena] Yes.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:56.013
- And that's super important.

00:07:56.013 --> 00:07:56.846
- Thank you.

00:07:56.846 --> 00:07:57.679
- Something super random.

00:07:57.679 --> 00:07:59.941
I hear, true or false,
you're a fan of "Shark Tank"?

00:07:59.941 --> 00:08:01.940
- Yes, I am.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:02.773
- True!

00:08:02.773 --> 00:08:03.980
- I am, that's very true.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.310
- Yeah, how did you get in?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.757
I know a lot of people
it's like, you either love

00:08:07.757 --> 00:08:09.560
"Shark Tank" or you've never seen it.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:11.118
It's like once you've seen it--

00:08:11.118 --> 00:08:12.120
- One episode, it's a tattoo.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.748
One episode and you're
never gonna go back.

00:08:13.748 --> 00:08:14.581
- It's addictive.

00:08:14.581 --> 00:08:16.570
- I'm just so, all of a
sudden I think I'm them.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.860
I'm like, royalties, that's a good one.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.040
Like I would just try to like chime in

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.280
as if I knew anything.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.570
But I realized I've owned half the things

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:26.403
that were--

00:08:26.403 --> 00:08:28.313
You guys probably owned half
the things they've created.

00:08:28.313 --> 00:08:29.146
'Cause I just--

00:08:29.146 --> 00:08:29.979
- [Kelly] Yeah, and I just don't know it.

00:08:29.979 --> 00:08:30.812
- I don't, exactly.

00:08:30.812 --> 00:08:32.860
It's been around for so
long that I have the sponge,

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.426
I got the comfy, I got the pillow.

00:08:35.426 --> 00:08:36.260
(laughing)

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.330
- You're like that old
lady at home, on like,

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.600
online shopping.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:40.512
- I'm like, gotta have that!

00:08:40.512 --> 00:08:41.345
(laughing)

00:08:41.345 --> 00:08:42.526
Definitely ordering that.

00:08:42.526 --> 00:08:43.380
(laughing)

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:44.370
- I need that.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.430
- Yeah, for some reason.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:48.140
- So your other thing is, which is funny

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:48.973
